{
  "requirement": "The bundled skills MUST direct agents to describe sites exactly as the site queries select them, to state as an obligation any convention the queries rely on, such as how a list is named, and to state only per-site obligations that a reviewer can check from the site and the helpers it calls.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject `requirements.cli.distributed_guidance.site_text` requires the bundled skills to direct agents to do three things. (1) They describe sites exactly as the site queries select them. (2) They state as an obligation any convention the queries rely on. (3) They state only per-site obligations that a reviewer can check from the site and the helpers it calls.\n\nThe only reviewed test is `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bundled_skills_describe_sites_as_queries_select_them_with_checkable_obligations]`. It reads the habeas skill's `references/distributed-requirements.md` through `distributed_reference`. `section` extracts the `## Do` and `## Don't` bodies. `assert_text` fails if any listed phrase is missing. I read all three helpers in the search results.\n\n- **Obligations 1 and 2.** The test asserts that `## Do` contains \"Describe sites exactly as the site queries select them. When a query relies on a convention, such as how a variable is named, state the convention as an obligation\". That covers both directives. The requirement's own example is \"how a list is named\", but it is introduced by \"such as\", so it only illustrates the rule.\n- **Obligation 1, negative form.** The test asserts that `## Don't` contains \"Don't describe sites more broadly than the queries select\".\n- **Obligation 3.** The test asserts that `## Don't` contains \"Don't state a per-site obligation that a reviewer cannot check from the site and the helpers it calls\". This is the checkability clause.\n\nThe requirement is about guidance text being present, so phrase-presence assertions scoped to the sections that hold the guidance are an appropriate check. A search of the bundled skills found this guidance only in `assets/skills/habeas/references/distributed-requirements.md`, which the test covers. Removing or rewording any of these directives would make the test fail. I found no uncovered obligation, no marking gap and no acknowledgment to assess.",
  "references": "8d24124587f48aa60c8910f00f280e5187ea855aff465ec50b2bcd288d4608d0",
